A||||2||Fret Naught||Fiero Saved my life||||4||
Z||000000||Fret Naught||01-09-2001||03:43 PM||||Sounds a bit dramatic I know, but I truely think it did, I was driving home yesterday on the freeway, not much traffic when the truck pulling a trailer up ahead of me lost what looked like part of a drive line or hitch or something, (BIG CHUNK OF STEEL) about 18 inches long bouncing on the road. It takes a bounce and is headed right for me, I mean me as in headed throung the windshield, so I just react, headed off on to the shoulder,  to get out of the way, and back on the road, the shoulder droppped off into a big ravine. At 70MPH she just stuck like glue responded to every command. I thought man if I were in my van or pickup it would have been all over. She got a good bath when I got home, and I decided to get started on that wood dash I have been promising. ||||reg||4
Z||000001||zeusrekning||01-09-2001||03:51 PM||||Glad to here you're ok. I rode my fiero down a hill off the side of the interstate. When the sun came out i noticed i was about 10 feet from a large chopped down tree, and if i went 25 ft farther down the road i would of went behind the gaurd rail and down in a huge gully. Fiero survived with very minor scratches.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||01-09-2001||07:12 PM||||Way to go.<BR>Bout a month ago I was going to work, in the afternoon, on a main hiway in Houston.  There was a little more traffic than usual, but you know Fieros: you can't see beyond the car ahead of you.  This was at the usual 70-80 mph.  The guy in front suddenly hit the brakes -hard- then swerved to the left lane, at the same time a car in front of him swerved to the right lane.  So in a fraction of an instant my mind registered that there was trouble ahead.  In the next fraction of the same instant I found myself about to have a snack on a minivan's rear bumper (3rd vehicle in front of me).  I braked and swerved to the left without having time to see if anybody was there.  As I passed the minivan I saw that it was a stepladder laying in the middle of the hiway, causing all this.<P>That exact same thing happened to me twice within about 4 weeks.  The first time I looked back and saw an 18-wheeler run over it and practically turned it into dust.<BR>     <P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
